==English==
{{wp}}

===Etymology===
{{der|en|NL.|-}}, from {{der|en|fr|urée}}, from {{der|en|grc|οὖρον||urine}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/jʊˈɹiːə/|/ˈjʊəɹɪə/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-urea.wav|Audio (Southern England)}}
* {{rhymes|en|iːə|s=3}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|organic compound|biochemistry|uncountable}} A water-soluble [[organic compound]], CO(NH<sub>2</sub>)<sub>2</sub>, formed by the [[metabolism]] of [[protein]]s and excreted in the [[urine]].
# {{lb|en|organic compound|countable}} Any ''N''-[[substituted]] [[derivative]] of urea, with the [[general formula]] (R<sub>1</sub>R<sub>2</sub>N)CO(NR<sub>3</sub>R<sub>4</sub>).

